# DFX production flow (fpga/dfx/Makefile): all Vivado work dirs live under
# fpga/dfx/build/ (already matched by the global `build/` rule above, listed
# here for explicitness). Overlay payloads (overlay/<rm>/*.bin) are large and
# regenerated by `make -C fpga/dfx overlays`; they are already matched by the
# global *.bin/*.ltx rules. overlay/<rm>/manifest.json is deliberately NOT
# ignored: manifests are small, commit-worthy build evidence — but note a
# fresh clone then fails `gen_manifest.py verify` until the payloads are
# regenerated (documented in fpga/dfx/README.md "Overlay triples").
#
# overlay_linux/ (the MBV-Linux harness's own overlay set) follows the SAME rule:
# manifests tracked, *.bin regenerated. Its manifests additionally carry
# static_usercode, which binds them to one static IMPLEMENTATION — see
# docs/PLATFORM_ONE_IMPL.md. Regenerating those payloads means re-running
# build_dfx.tcl, which re-mints that identity, so a regenerated set is NOT
# interchangeable with a fielded one.
fpga/dfx/build/
# OOC synthesis scratch for the B2 nanosoc variant (checkpoints + reports,
# reproducible from fpga/rp/nanosoc/ooc_synth.tcl with SOCSCOPE=1).
fpga/rp/nanosoc/build_b2/

# Host-gcc test-harness binaries (I27): rebuilt by `make -C firmware/test`;
# the six b3e8e99-era binaries were untracked at the batch-3 checkpoint.
firmware/test/bin/

# --- added 2026-07-09 -------------------------------------------------------
# Vivado/DFX scratch build dirs beyond the plain `build/` rule above.
# `fpga/dfx/build512/` is ~88 MB of place-and-route scratch — never commit it.
fpga/dfx/build*/
# fpga/rp/nanosoc_iice: Synplify/Identify scratch. The bare `build/` rule above
# catches the default OUT, but the Makefile's OUT is overridable (e.g.
# OUT=.../build_noiice for the uninstrumented cost-comparison build), and a
# Synplify rev dir is ~58 MB of .srm/.srr/.edf. Same `build*/` shape as the two
# neighbouring rules. Sources, .fdc, .idc and vsrc_override/ live outside build*.
fpga/rp/nanosoc_iice/build*/
.srcs/

# Simulation run+build artefacts, repo-wide (cocotb Makefile.sim + direct VCS).
# Generic so ANY new bench dir — under tests/ or elsewhere — is covered without
# needing its own .gitignore. Only artefact classes that ACTUALLY occur in this
# tree are listed. NOTE: this block used to say "no *.fsdb/novas*/verdi* — none
# are present, so not speculated". That is no longer true — tests/identify_iice
# introduced the repo's first FSDB dumping (Verdi/nCompare trace comparison), so
# those classes are now listed below for real. Sources/evidence (*.sv, *.py, Makefile,
# RESULT.txt) are NOT matched and stay committable. This subsumes the former
# per-dir rules for tests/rmii_conformance/{csrc,simv*,ucli.key} (its *.log go
# via the global *.log rule) and mirrors the tracked tests/.gitignore per-block
# list one level up so it also applies outside tests/.
sim_build/
results.xml
ucli.key
csrc/
vc_hdrs.h
*.daidir/
simv
simv_*

# Verdi / FSDB artefacts — introduced by tests/identify_iice (the repo's first
# FSDB flow). The *Log/ rule covers the dirs every Verdi utility drops into the
# CWD: nCompareLog/, verdiLog/, fsdbqryLog/, fsdbdirLog/, fsdb2vcdLog/.
*.fsdb
*.fsdb.*
*.vcd
*.vpd
*.nce
DVEfiles/
AN.DB/
novas*
verdi*
*Log/
.vlogansetup.*
# identify_debugger_shell rotates its log into the CWD: identdebugger.log plus
# .bak, .bak.1, .bak.2 ... The bare .log goes via the global *.log rule above;
# these rotations do not. Same CWD-litter class as the *Log/ dirs.
identdebugger.log*
# ... and both the Identify debugger and Synplify drop a synlog.tcl transcript
# into whatever CWD they were launched from (seen in the repo root and in
# host/identify/ after running debug_session.tcl). It is a replayable command
# log, never an input, and it is NOT covered by any rule above. Unanchored on
# purpose: the CWD depends on where the tool was invoked.
synlog.tcl

# poc/systemrdl: sources + evidence (rdl/*.rdl, *.py, tb/*.sv, RESULT/EQUIV*.txt,
# *.patch) are committed. Build outputs are regenerated by `make -C poc/systemrdl`
# (its clean target removes: generated/ compat/ __pycache__ sim sim_*). __pycache__
# is already covered by the global Python rule; sim*/ covers the poc `sim/`+`sim_*`
# equivalence work dirs that the generic sim_build/ above does not.
poc/systemrdl/generated/
poc/systemrdl/compat/
poc/systemrdl/sim*/

# poc/ddr4_mbv: sources (*.tcl, *.py, *.xdc, *.csv, Makefile, fw/*.{S,c,ld}) +
# the RESULT.txt evidence are committed; build/ is the 280 MB Vivado scratch
# (DCPs/IP/logs, already caught by the global build/ rule). These are the loose
# MicroBlaze fw build outputs the global rules do NOT catch — regenerable via
# fw/Makefile.
poc/ddr4_mbv/fw/*.o
poc/ddr4_mbv/fw/*.elf
poc/ddr4_mbv/fw/*.bin
poc/ddr4_mbv/fw/*.map
poc/ddr4_mbv/fw/*.lst

# --- src/linux_soc (feat/linux-mps3-fabric): heavy, fully regenerable trees ---
# Keep 'git status' a lean, reviewable diff. Sources (*.tcl,*.sv,*.c,*.S,*.ld,
# *.xdc,*.py,Makefile), RESULT.txt/*.rpt evidence, MANIFEST.txt and docs stay
# committable; the multi-hundred-MB build/sim/package binaries below do not.
#
# DDR4 memtest xsim co-sim scratch (~120 MB EACH: build_tlm, build_v2..v7,
# bfm_char's snb0/tlm_snb0 run dirs). The global 'build/' rule already catches
# fw_memtest/build/ but NOT the versioned dirs, so name them explicitly.
src/linux_soc/fw_memtest/build*/
src/linux_soc/fw_memtest/bfm_char/snb*/
src/linux_soc/fw_memtest/bfm_char/tlm_snb*/
# Vivado hw build scratch is already covered by the global build/ + *.bit/
# *.xsa/*.dcp rules (incl. build/STALE_PRE_DDR4FIX/); listed for explicitness.
src/linux_soc/hw/build/

